BT /F2 8.5 Tf 39.69 513.64 Td (GAP EFFECTS ON THIS DRAWING AND THE SCREEN) Tj ET
BT /F1 5.39 Tf 42.52 500.6 Td (G-eccs-success: ECCS success criterion \(how many RVVs and RRVs must open\) -> ECCS is screened only for supports every valve train shares \(valid for any success criterion\); no k-of-n single-failure screen) Tj ET
BT /F1 5.39 Tf 42.52 490.68 Td (G-dhrs-valves: DHRS actuation / isolation valve count and type per train -> each train is modelled as one valve group + one condenser; no NUREG/CR-6928 data row can be matched) Tj ET
BT /F1 5.39 Tf 42.52 480.76 Td (G-dc: non-Class 1E DC system architecture \(common vs module-specific, divisions, battery duration\) -> multi-module actuation on loss of a shared DC supply is not determinable) Tj ET
BT /F1 5.39 Tf 42.52 470.83 Td (G-mps: module protection system separation groups / divisions and their power -> MPS modelled as one actuating system per module; channel independence not screened) Tj ET
BT /F1 5.39 Tf 42.52 460.91 Td (G-layout: building, room and fire-area layout of DHRS / ECCS equipment -> spatial common-cause \(fire, flood\) not screened) Tj ET
BT /F1 5.39 Tf 42.52 450.99 Td (G-pool-inventory: pool inventory, level limits and heat-up / boil-off times for the US600 -> the shared heat sink is a structural dependency only; no time to boil) Tj ET
BT /F1 5.39 Tf 42.52 441.07 Td (G-dimensions: US600 building, pool, bay and containment dimensions and the bay arrangement -> the facility GA is schematic: the only dimensions drawn are the secondary, design-family values \(CNV 76 ft x 19 ft, bay 20 ft square x 53 ft deep\), labelled S2; the bay arrangement, building outline and pool-to-grade elevation are UNKNOWN) Tj ET
BT /F1 5.39 Tf 42.52 431.15 Td (G-reliability: failure data for passive components \(condensers, pool, building\) and NuScale valve designs -> fault and event trees are built and their cut sets computed; nothing is quantified) Tj ET
